If you really want a crappy valk, try a cavewoman, and if you're
craving a wimpier magic user, go for a healer.  And if you're not fond
of your starting equipment, try out a tourist.

It seems to me that, in general, Nethack is a bit too difficult in the
early game and much too easy in the late game.  Voluntary challenges
seem to mostly address the ease of the late game.  Illiteracy doesn't
hurt you much early on, when you wouldn't have many scrolls or know
what they are anyway, but later on, not being able to genocide or max
out your armor and weapons adds a significant level of difficult to
the endgame.

The patch you describe would make the game only harder until the
player exercized a bit, found a luckstone, and maybe a potion or two
of gain ability.

If someone were going to write a challenge patch, I think it would be
better balance-wise to focus on changes that would make you a little
less invulnerable once you've gotten together an AK.

